    {
      "id": "location",
      "prose_links": [
        {
          "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States#Geography",
          "lang": "en",
          "text": "Geography"
        }
      ],
      "prose_text": {
        "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States#Geography",
        "html": "The United States is the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_and_dependencies_by_area\">third or fourth largest country</a> by total area,<sup data-note=\"7\"></sup><sup data-note=\"8\"></sup> with figures ranging between 3,717,813 and 3,809,525 square miles (9,629,091 and 9,866,624 km2).<sup data-note=\"7\"></sup><sup data-note=\"9\"></sup>",
        "lang": "en",
        "local": true,
        "title": "Geography"
      },
      "title": {
        "href": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1071",
        "lang": "en",
        "text": "geography"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "government",
      "prose_links": [],
      "prose_text": null,
      "title": {
        "href": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7188",
        "lang": "en",
        "text": "government"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "demography",
      "prose_links": [
        {
          "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States#Demographics",
          "lang": "en",
          "text": "Demographics"
        }
      ],
      "prose_text": {
        "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States#Demographics",
        "html": "The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Census_Bureau\">U.S. Census Bureau</a> reported 331,449,281 residents on April 1, 2020,<sup data-note=\"10\"></sup><sup data-note=\"11\"></sup> making the United States the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_and_dependencies_by_population\">third-most-populous country</a> in the world, after India and China.<sup data-note=\"12\"></sup> The Census Bureau's official 2025 population estimate was 341,784,857, an increase of 3.1% since the 2020 census.<sup data-note=\"13\"></sup> According to the Bureau's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._and_World_Population_Clock\">U.S. Population Clock</a>, on July 1, 2024, the U.S. population had a net gain of one person every 16 seconds, or about 5400 people per day.<sup data-note=\"14\"></sup> In 2023, 51% of Americans age 15 and over were married, 6% were <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Widowed\">widowed</a>, 10% were divorced, and 34% had never been married.<sup data-note=\"15\"></sup> In 2023, the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Total_fertility_rate\">total fertility rate</a> for the U.S. stood at 1.6 children per woman,<sup data-note=\"16\"></sup> and, at 23%, it had the world's highest rate of children living in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Single_parents_in_the_United_States\">single-parent</a> households in 2019.<sup data-note=\"17\"></sup> Most Americans live in the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suburb\">suburbs</a> of major metropolitan areas.",
        "lang": "en",
        "local": true,
        "title": "Demographics"
      },
      "title": {
        "href": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q37732",
        "lang": "en",
        "text": "demography"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "economy",
      "prose_links": [
        {
          "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States#Economy",
          "lang": "en",
          "text": "Economy"
        }
      ],
      "prose_text": {
        "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States#Economy",
        "html": "The U.S. has a highly developed <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mixed_economy\">mixed economy</a><sup data-note=\"18\"></sup> that has been the world's largest nominally <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_largest_historical_GDP\">since about 1890</a>.<sup data-note=\"19\"></sup> Its 2024 <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gross_domestic_product\">gross domestic product</a> (GDP)<sup data-note=\"20\"></sup> of more than $29 trillion<sup data-note=\"21\"></sup> constituted over 25% of nominal <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gross_world_product\">global economic output</a>, or 15% at <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purchasing_power_parity\">purchasing power parity</a> (PPP). The country ranks <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_(nominal)\">first in the world by nominal GDP</a>,<sup data-note=\"22\"></sup> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_(PPP)\">second when adjusted for purchasing power parities</a> (PPP),<sup data-note=\"23\"></sup> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_countries_by_GDP_(PPP)_per_capita\">ninth by PPP-adjusted GDP per capita</a>.<sup data-note=\"23\"></sup> In August 2026, the total <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_debt_of_the_United_States\">U.S. federal government debt</a> passed $40 trillion, having more than doubled in the previous decade.<sup data-note=\"24\"></sup>",
        "lang": "en",
        "local": true,
        "title": "Economy"
      },
      "title": {
        "href": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q159810",
        "lang": "en",
        "text": "economy"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "development",
      "prose_links": [],
      "prose_text": null,
      "title": {
        "href": "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4810841",
        "lang": "en",
        "text": "socioeconomic development"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "infrastructure",
      "prose_links": [],
      "prose_text": null,
